 "examples": [
  {
   "question": "A closed-loop system has transfer function G(s) = 25/(s² + 6s + 25). Find ωn, ζ, the damped frequency ωd, the peak overshoot in percent, and the peak time.",
   "steps": [
    "Compare the denominator with s² + 2ζωn s + ωn². The constant term gives ωn² = 25, so ωn = 5 rad/s.",
    "The coefficient of s gives 2ζωn = 6, so ζ = 6/(2 × 5) = 0.6.",
    "Since 0 < 0.6 < 1, the system is underdamped and the sine forms apply.",
    "√(1 − ζ²) = √(1 − 0.36) = √0.64 = 0.8.",
    "ωd = ωn√(1 − ζ²) = 5 × 0.8 = 4 rad/s. Also φ = cos⁻¹ 0.6 = 0.9273 rad.",
    "Peak overshoot Mp = e^(−πζ/√(1−ζ²)) = e^(−π × 0.6/0.8) = e^(−2.3562) = 0.0948, that is 9.48%.",
    "Peak time tp = π/ωd = π/4 = 0.7854 s, about 0.785 s."
   ],
   "answer": "ωn = 5 rad/s, ζ = 0.6 (underdamped), ωd = 4 rad/s, peak overshoot 9.48%, peak time 0.785 s.",
   "check": "import math\nwn = math.sqrt(25)\nzeta = 6/(2*wn)\nwd = wn*math.sqrt(1-zeta**2)\nMp = 100*math.exp(-math.pi*zeta/math.sqrt(1-zeta**2))\ntp = math.pi/wd\nprint(round(wn,3))\nprint(round(zeta,3))\nprint(round(wd,3))\nprint(round(Mp,2))\nprint(round(tp,3))",
   "values": [
    5.0,
    0.6,
    4.0,
    9.48,
    0.785
   ],
   "output": ""
  }
